window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a466-90841d0c1fa15b5f.json"]={sha256:"90841d0c1fa15b5f3e06106c4205fb562b0e8bec329a827e7245de2d6d11bf3c",value:{"id":"a466","title":"時間投影室偵測器","titleEn":"Time-projection-chamber detectors","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以 CERN ALICE 的 90 m³ 時間投影室為範本：從 400 V/cm 下的電子漂移與擴散，到四層 GEM 讀出的增益與離子回流，再把雷射、氪校正、空間電荷畸變圖與 524,160 通道的連續讀出整合成可交接的偵測器效能紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using the 90 m³ ALICE TPC at CERN as the template: from electron drift and diffusion at 400 V/cm, through gain and ion back-flow of four-GEM readout, to laser and krypton calibration, space-charge distortion maps and continuous readout of 524,160 channels, integrated into a transferable detector performance record.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-accelerators-detectors","subcategoryTitle":"加速器、光束線與粒子偵測器","subcategoryTitleEn":"Accelerators, beamlines and particle detectors","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-accelerators-detectors","learningTags":["optics","optics-accelerators-detectors","detector"],"architectureFamily":"detector","architectureNodes":[["中央電極與場籠","Central electrode and field cage"],["漂移氣體體積","Drift gas volume"],["四層 GEM 讀出室","Four-GEM readout chambers"],["SAMPA 前端與光纖讀出","SAMPA front end and optical readout"],["雷射與氪校正","Laser and krypton calibration"],["軌跡重建與畸變修正","Track reconstruction and distortion correction"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,5],[4,1],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"detector","labels":["中央電極與場籠","漂移氣體體積","四層 GEM 讀出室","SAMPA 前端與光纖讀出","雷射與氪校正"],"labelsEn":["Central electrode and field cage","Drift gas volume","Four-GEM readout chambers","SAMPA front end and optical readout","Laser and krypton calibration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"漂移與定位練習：假設 ALICE TPC 以 400 V/cm、v_d = 2.58 cm/µs 運作，一條軌跡在距讀出面 200 cm 處產生叢集。到達時間 t = 200/2.58 ≈ 77.5 µs，以 5 MHz 取樣為 388 個時間格。取 D'_T = 220 µm/√cm，橫向擴散 σ_T = 220×√200 ≈ 3.1 mm；一列 7.5 mm 墊片約收集 30 個初級電子，重心的統計極限為 3.1/√30 ≈ 0.57 mm，再與墊片響應加雜訊項（假設 0.5 mm）平方相加得約 0.76 mm，接近實測的 0.8 mm 等級。若氣體溫度上升讓漂移速度加快 0.3%，未校正的 z 偏差為 200 cm × 0.003 = 6 mm，已是位置解析度的 8 倍，這說明為何漂移速度必須連續監測。數值為教學假設，不代表實驗的正式規格。","textEn":"Drift-and-position exercise: assume the ALICE TPC runs at 400 V/cm with v_d = 2.58 cm/µs and a track produces a cluster 200 cm from the readout plane. Arrival time t = 200/2.58 ≈ 77.5 µs, i.e. 388 time bins at 5 MHz sampling. With D'_T = 220 µm/√cm the transverse diffusion is σ_T = 220×√200 ≈ 3.1 mm; a 7.5 mm pad row collects about 30 primary electrons, so the centroid statistical limit is 3.1/√30 ≈ 0.57 mm, and adding a pad-response-plus-noise term of 0.5 mm in quadrature gives about 0.76 mm, close to the measured 0.8 mm class. If a gas temperature rise speeds the drift by 0.3%, the uncorrected z error is 200 cm × 0.003 = 6 mm, eight times the position resolution, which is why drift velocity must be monitored continuously. Values are teaching assumptions, not the experiment's formal specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a466-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「游離、漂移與時間投影原理」與「擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle\" and \"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a466-v12-01","title":"游離、漂移與時間投影原理：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「中央電極與漂移體積」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Central electrode and drift volume” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"帶電粒子穿過氣體時沿軌跡產生初級游離電子團。ALICE TPC 把中央電極保持在 −100 kV，兩端的讀出平面接近地電位，形成 400 V/cm 的軸向電場，電子以 2.58 cm/µs 的速度向端板漂移；墊片的二維位置給出 x、y，到達時間乘以漂移速度給出 z，三維軌跡因此由「把時間投影成空間」重建。Ne-CO₂-N₂（90-10-5）混合氣兼顧低原子序（多重散射小）、足夠的初級游離密度與較低的離子回流。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「中央電極與漂移體積」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A charged particle crossing the gas leaves clusters of primary ionisation along its path. The ALICE TPC holds its central electrode at −100 kV with the two end-plate readout planes near ground, creating a 400 V/cm axial field along which electrons drift at 2.58 cm/µs; the two-dimensional pad position gives x and y, and arrival time multiplied by drift velocity gives z, so the three-dimensional track is reconstructed by projecting time into space. The Ne-CO₂-N₂ (90-10-5) mixture balances low atomic number for little multiple scattering, adequate primary ionisation density and low ion back-flow. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Central electrode and drift volume”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm；最長漂移時間 t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs；取 W ≈ 38 eV、最小游離能損約 1.5 keV/cm，每公分約產生 40 個電子，一列 7.5 mm 的墊片約收集 30 個初級電子。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm; the longest drift time is t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs; with W ≈ 38 eV and a minimum-ionising loss of about 1.5 keV/cm the gas yields roughly 40 electrons per cm, so a 7.5 mm pad row collects about 30 primary electrons.","failure":"常見誤解：「電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「中央電極與漂移體積」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Central electrode and drift volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-01-k1","title":"游離、漂移與時間投影原理","titleEn":"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle","text":"帶電粒子穿過氣體時沿軌跡產生初級游離電子團。ALICE TPC 把中央電極保持在 −100 kV，兩端的讀出平面接近地電位，形成 400 V/cm 的軸向電場，電子以 2.58 cm/µs 的速度向端板漂移；墊片的二維位置給出 x、y，到達時間乘以漂移速度給出 z，三維軌跡因此由「把時間投影成空間」重建。","textEn":"A charged particle crossing the gas leaves clusters of primary ionisation along its path. The ALICE TPC holds its central electrode at −100 kV with the two end-plate readout planes near ground, creating a 400 V/cm axial field along which electrons drift at 2.58 cm/µs; the two-dimensional pad position gives x and y, and arrival time multiplied by drift velocity gives z, so the three-dimensional track is reconstructed by projecting time into space.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「游離、漂移與時間投影原理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle\" is correct?","options":["電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","帶電粒子穿過氣體時沿軌跡產生初級游離電子團。","磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","A charged particle crossing the gas leaves clusters of primary ionisation along its path.","The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帶電粒子穿過氣體時沿軌跡產生初級游離電子團。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A charged particle crossing the gas leaves clusters of primary ionisation along its path. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a466-v12-02","title":"游離、漂移與時間投影原理：定量估算","titleEn":"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「中央電極與漂移體積」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Central electrode and drift volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm；最長漂移時間 t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs；取 W ≈ 38 eV、最小游離能損約 1.5 keV/cm，每公分約產生 40 個電子，一列 7.5 mm 的墊片約收集 30 個初級電子。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm; the longest drift time is t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs; with W ≈ 38 eV and a minimum-ionising loss of about 1.5 keV/cm the gas yields roughly 40 electrons per cm, so a 7.5 mm pad row collects about 30 primary electrons. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：由中央電極電壓與漂移長度算出場強與 t_max，再與雷射軌跡或宇宙射線事件中觀察到的最大到達時間比較（5 MHz 取樣下約 485 個時間格）；z 座標的線性以位置已知的雷射束驗證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute the field and t_max from the electrode voltage and drift length, then compare with the latest arrival times seen in laser or cosmic-ray events (about 485 time bins at 5 MHz sampling); check z linearity with laser beams at known positions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm；最長漂移時間 t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs；取 W ≈ 38 eV、最小游離能損約 1.5 keV/cm，每公分約產生 40 個電子，一列 7.5 mm 的墊片約收集 30 個初級電子。","textEn":"E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm; the longest drift time is t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs; with W ≈ 38 eV and a minimum-ionising loss of about 1.5 keV/cm the gas yields roughly 40 electrons per cm, so a 7.5 mm pad row collects about 30 primary electrons.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「游離、漂移與時間投影原理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle\", which statement holds?","options":["氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。","對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。","E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm。"],"optionsEn":["Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.","A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.","E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm；最長漂移時間 t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs；取 W ≈ 38 eV、最小游離能損約 1.5 keV/cm，每公分約產生 40 個電子，一列 7.5 mm 的墊片約收集 30 個初級電子。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"E = V/L = 100 kV/250 cm = 400 V/cm; the longest drift time is t_max = L/v_d = 250 cm ÷ 2.58 cm/µs ≈ 97 µs; with W ≈ 38 eV and a minimum-ionising loss of about 1.5 keV/cm the gas yields roughly 40 electrons per cm, so a 7.5 mm pad row collects about 30 primary electrons. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a466-v12-03","title":"游離、漂移與時間投影原理：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「中央電極與漂移體積」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Central electrode and drift volume” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"由中央電極電壓與漂移長度算出場強與 t_max，再與雷射軌跡或宇宙射線事件中觀察到的最大到達時間比較（5 MHz 取樣下約 485 個時間格）；z 座標的線性以位置已知的雷射束驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute the field and t_max from the electrode voltage and drift length, then compare with the latest arrival times seen in laser or cosmic-ray events (about 485 time bins at 5 MHz sampling); check z linearity with laser beams at known positions. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若假設的漂移速度錯 1%，全長漂移的 z 座標偏 2.5 cm，TPC 兩半的軌跡在中央電極處無法對接，頂點與動量重建都失真。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A 1% error in the assumed drift velocity displaces full-drift z by 2.5 cm, so tracks from the two TPC halves fail to match at the central electrode and both vertex and momentum reconstruction degrade.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由中央電極電壓與漂移長度算出場強與 t_max，再與雷射軌跡或宇宙射線事件中觀察到的最大到達時間比較（5 MHz 取樣下約 485 個時間格）；z 座標的線性以位置已知的雷射束驗證。","textEn":"Compute the field and t_max from the electrode voltage and drift length, then compare with the latest arrival times seen in laser or cosmic-ray events (about 485 time bins at 5 MHz sampling); check z linearity with laser beams at known positions.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「游離、漂移與時間投影原理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle\"?","options":["由中央電極電壓與漂移長度算出場強與 t_max，再與雷射軌跡或宇宙射線事件中觀察到的最大到達時間比較（5 MHz 取樣下約 485 個時間格）。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。"],"optionsEn":["Compute the field and t_max from the electrode voltage and drift length, then compare with the latest arrival times seen in laser or cosmic-ray events (about 485 time bins at 5 MHz sampling).","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"由中央電極電壓與漂移長度算出場強與 t_max，再與雷射軌跡或宇宙射線事件中觀察到的最大到達時間比較（5 MHz 取樣下約 485 個時間格）；z 座標的線性以位置已知的雷射束驗證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute the field and t_max from the electrode voltage and drift length, then compare with the latest arrival times seen in laser or cosmic-ray events (about 485 time bins at 5 MHz sampling); check z linearity with laser beams at known positions. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a466-v12-04","title":"游離、漂移與時間投影原理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「中央電極與漂移體積」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Central electrode and drift volume” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若假設的漂移速度錯 1%，全長漂移的 z 座標偏 2.5 cm，TPC 兩半的軌跡在中央電極處無法對接，頂點與動量重建都失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A 1% error in the assumed drift velocity displaces full-drift z by 2.5 cm, so tracks from the two TPC halves fail to match at the central electrode and both vertex and momentum reconstruction degrade. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：Ne-CO₂-N₂（90-10-5）混合氣兼顧低原子序（多重散射小）、足夠的初級游離密度與較低的離子回流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Ne-CO₂-N₂ (90-10-5) mixture balances low atomic number for little multiple scattering, adequate primary ionisation density and low ion back-flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若假設的漂移速度錯 1%，全長漂移的 z 座標偏 2.5 cm，TPC 兩半的軌跡在中央電極處無法對接，頂點與動量重建都失真。","textEn":"A 1% error in the assumed drift velocity displaces full-drift z by 2.5 cm, so tracks from the two TPC halves fail to match at the central electrode and both vertex and momentum reconstruction degrade.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「游離、漂移與時間投影原理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ionisation, drift and the time-projection principle\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","若假設的漂移速度錯 1%，全長漂移的 z 座標偏 2.5 cm，TPC 兩半的軌跡在中央電極處無法對接，頂點與動量重建都失真。","磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","A 1% error in the assumed drift velocity displaces full-drift z by 2.5 cm, so tracks from the two TPC halves fail to match at the central electrode and both vertex and momentum reconstruction degrade.","The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若假設的漂移速度錯 1%，全長漂移的 z 座標偏 2.5 cm，TPC 兩半的軌跡在中央電極處無法對接，頂點與動量重建都失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A 1% error in the assumed drift velocity displaces full-drift z by 2.5 cm, so tracks from the two TPC halves fail to match at the central electrode and both vertex and momentum reconstruction degrade. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a466-v12-05","title":"擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「擴散與磁場」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion and magnetic field” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"漂移中的電子不斷與氣體分子碰撞，電子雲以隨機走動方式散開，橫向與縱向寬度都隨漂移時間按 √(2Dt) 成長，工程上常寫成 σ = D'·√L，D' 的單位是 µm/√cm。ALICE 的 0.5 T 螺線管磁場讓電子在兩次碰撞之間繞磁力線迴旋，橫向擴散按 1/√(1+ω²τ²) 縮小，縱向擴散則不受影響。擴散決定電子團抵達讀出面時的尺寸，再除以電子數的平方根才是重心定位的統計極限。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「擴散與磁場」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A drifting electron collides continuously with gas molecules, so the electron cloud spreads as a random walk whose transverse and longitudinal widths grow as √(2Dt), usually written σ = D'·√L with D' in µm/√cm. The 0.5 T solenoid field of ALICE makes electrons gyrate between collisions, shrinking transverse diffusion by 1/√(1+ω²τ²) while leaving longitudinal diffusion unchanged. Diffusion fixes the size of the cloud reaching the pad plane, and dividing that width by the square root of the electron count gives the statistical limit of centroid positioning. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Diffusion and magnetic field”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：取 D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm（教學假設），全長 250 cm 漂移後 σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm；改寫成 σ² = 2Dt，D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s；縱向的 3.5 mm 對應時間展寬 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns；30 個電子的重心極限約 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm (teaching assumption), a full 250 cm drift gives σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm; in the form σ² = 2Dt this is D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s; the longitudinal 3.5 mm corresponds to a time spread of 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns, and the centroid limit for 30 electrons is about 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「擴散與磁場」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Diffusion and magnetic field”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-05-k1","title":"擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限","titleEn":"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit","text":"漂移中的電子不斷與氣體分子碰撞，電子雲以隨機走動方式散開，橫向與縱向寬度都隨漂移時間按 √(2Dt) 成長，工程上常寫成 σ = D'·√L，D' 的單位是 µm/√cm。ALICE 的 0.5 T 螺線管磁場讓電子在兩次碰撞之間繞磁力線迴旋，橫向擴散按 1/√(1+ω²τ²) 縮小，縱向擴散則不受影響。","textEn":"A drifting electron collides continuously with gas molecules, so the electron cloud spreads as a random walk whose transverse and longitudinal widths grow as √(2Dt), usually written σ = D'·√L with D' in µm/√cm. The 0.5 T solenoid field of ALICE makes electrons gyrate between collisions, shrinking transverse diffusion by 1/√(1+ω²τ²) while leaving longitudinal diffusion unchanged.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit\" is correct?","options":["磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。","漂移中的電子不斷與氣體分子碰撞，電子雲以隨機走動方式散開，橫向與縱向寬度都隨漂移時間按 √(2Dt) 成長，工程上常寫成 σ = D'·√L，D' 的單位是 µm/√cm。"],"optionsEn":["The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion.","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.","A drifting electron collides continuously with gas molecules, so the electron cloud spreads as a random walk whose transverse and longitudinal widths grow as √(2Dt), usually written σ = D'·√L with D' in µm/√cm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漂移中的電子不斷與氣體分子碰撞，電子雲以隨機走動方式散開，橫向與縱向寬度都隨漂移時間按 √(2Dt) 成長，工程上常寫成 σ = D'·√L，D' 的單位是 µm/√cm。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A drifting electron collides continuously with gas molecules, so the electron cloud spreads as a random walk whose transverse and longitudinal widths grow as √(2Dt), usually written σ = D'·√L with D' in µm/√cm. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a466-v12-06","title":"擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限：定量估算","titleEn":"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散與磁場」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion and magnetic field” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：取 D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm（教學假設），全長 250 cm 漂移後 σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm；改寫成 σ² = 2Dt，D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s；縱向的 3.5 mm 對應時間展寬 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns；30 個電子的重心極限約 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm (teaching assumption), a full 250 cm drift gives σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm; in the form σ² = 2Dt this is D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s; the longitudinal 3.5 mm corresponds to a time spread of 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns, and the centroid limit for 30 electrons is about 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用雷射軌跡或宇宙射線量電子團在墊片方向與時間方向的寬度隨漂移長度的變化，擬合 σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L 取得 D'，並與 Magboltz 類模擬值比較；再比對磁場開啟與關閉時橫向寬度的差異。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure cluster width along pads and along time as a function of drift length with laser or cosmic tracks, fit σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L to extract D' and compare with Magboltz-type simulation; then compare transverse widths with the magnet on and off.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"取 D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm（教學假設），全長 250 cm 漂移後 σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm；改寫成 σ² = 2Dt，D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s；縱向的 3.5 mm 對應時間展寬 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns；30 個電子的重心極限約 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm。","textEn":"With D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm (teaching assumption), a full 250 cm drift gives σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm; in the form σ² = 2Dt this is D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s; the longitudinal 3.5 mm corresponds to a time spread of 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns, and the centroid limit for 30 electrons is about 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit\", which statement holds?","options":["取 D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm（教學假設），全長 250 cm 漂移後 σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm。","漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。","連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。"],"optionsEn":["With D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm (teaching assumption), a full 250 cm drift gives σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm.","Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough.","Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取 D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm（教學假設），全長 250 cm 漂移後 σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm；改寫成 σ² = 2Dt，D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s；縱向的 3.5 mm 對應時間展寬 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns；30 個電子的重心極限約 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With D'_T = D'_L = 220 µm/√cm (teaching assumption), a full 250 cm drift gives σ_T = 220×√250 ≈ 3.5 mm; in the form σ² = 2Dt this is D = (0.348 cm)²/(2×96.9 µs) ≈ 620 cm²/s; the longitudinal 3.5 mm corresponds to a time spread of 3.5 mm ÷ 25.8 mm/µs ≈ 135 ns, and the centroid limit for 30 electrons is about 3.5 mm/√30 ≈ 0.64 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a466-v12-07","title":"擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「擴散與磁場」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Diffusion and magnetic field” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用雷射軌跡或宇宙射線量電子團在墊片方向與時間方向的寬度隨漂移長度的變化，擬合 σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L 取得 D'，並與 Magboltz 類模擬值比較；再比對磁場開啟與關閉時橫向寬度的差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure cluster width along pads and along time as a function of drift length with laser or cosmic tracks, fit σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L to extract D' and compare with Magboltz-type simulation; then compare transverse widths with the magnet on and off. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：水氣或氧污染改變電子的碰撞特性，擴散係數與漂移速度一起漂移，電子團變寬、信號變矮，遠端漂移叢集的位置解析度與 dE/dx 同時變差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Water or oxygen contamination alters electron collision properties, so diffusion and drift velocity shift together; clusters broaden and signals shrink, degrading both position resolution and dE/dx for long-drift clusters.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用雷射軌跡或宇宙射線量電子團在墊片方向與時間方向的寬度隨漂移長度的變化，擬合 σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L 取得 D'，並與 Magboltz 類模擬值比較；再比對磁場開啟與關閉時橫向寬度的差異。","textEn":"Measure cluster width along pads and along time as a function of drift length with laser or cosmic tracks, fit σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L to extract D' and compare with Magboltz-type simulation; then compare transverse widths with the magnet on and off.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","用雷射軌跡或宇宙射線量電子團在墊片方向與時間方向的寬度隨漂移長度的變化，擬合 σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L 取得 D'，並與 Magboltz 類模擬值比較。","每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Measure cluster width along pads and along time as a function of drift length with laser or cosmic tracks, fit σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L to extract D' and compare with Magboltz-type simulation.","If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用雷射軌跡或宇宙射線量電子團在墊片方向與時間方向的寬度隨漂移長度的變化，擬合 σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L 取得 D'，並與 Magboltz 類模擬值比較；再比對磁場開啟與關閉時橫向寬度的差異。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure cluster width along pads and along time as a function of drift length with laser or cosmic tracks, fit σ² = σ₀² + D'²·L to extract D' and compare with Magboltz-type simulation; then compare transverse widths with the magnet on and off. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a466-v12-08","title":"擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散與磁場」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Diffusion and magnetic field” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"水氣或氧污染改變電子的碰撞特性，擴散係數與漂移速度一起漂移，電子團變寬、信號變矮，遠端漂移叢集的位置解析度與 dE/dx 同時變差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Water or oxygen contamination alters electron collision properties, so diffusion and drift velocity shift together; clusters broaden and signals shrink, degrading both position resolution and dE/dx for long-drift clusters. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：擴散決定電子團抵達讀出面時的尺寸，再除以電子數的平方根才是重心定位的統計極限。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Diffusion fixes the size of the cloud reaching the pad plane, and dividing that width by the square root of the electron count gives the statistical limit of centroid positioning.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水氣或氧污染改變電子的碰撞特性，擴散係數與漂移速度一起漂移，電子團變寬、信號變矮，遠端漂移叢集的位置解析度與 dE/dx 同時變差。","textEn":"Water or oxygen contamination alters electron collision properties, so diffusion and drift velocity shift together; clusters broaden and signals shrink, degrading both position resolution and dE/dx for long-drift clusters.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擴散、磁場與位置解析度極限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diffusion, magnetic field and the resolution limit\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。","水氣或氧污染改變電子的碰撞特性，擴散係數與漂移速度一起漂移，電子團變寬、信號變矮，遠端漂移叢集的位置解析度與 dE/dx 同時變差。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.","Water or oxygen contamination alters electron collision properties, so diffusion and drift velocity shift together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水氣或氧污染改變電子的碰撞特性，擴散係數與漂移速度一起漂移，電子團變寬、信號變矮，遠端漂移叢集的位置解析度與 dE/dx 同時變差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Water or oxygen contamination alters electron collision properties, so diffusion and drift velocity shift together; clusters broaden and signals shrink, degrading both position resolution and dE/dx for long-drift clusters. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a466-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「場籠、高壓與氣體純度」與「GEM 氣體增益與離子回流」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity\" and \"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a466-v12-09","title":"場籠、高壓與氣體純度：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「場籠與電阻鏈」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Field cage and resistor chain” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"場籠用鍍鋁 Mylar 條帶環繞漂移體積，由電阻鏈把 −100 kV 逐級分壓，讓每一條帶的電位落在理想的線性分佈上，電場才能在 2.5 m 的全長保持均勻；靠近讀出面另有裙狀電極修正端部場。氣體系統以閉迴路循環並連續純化，氧與水必須壓在 ppm 等級，否則電子被電負性分子吸附而消失，而且漂移速度會隨 E/N、溫度與壓力改變。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「場籠與電阻鏈」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The field cage surrounds the drift volume with aluminised Mylar strips whose potentials are set by a resistor chain dividing the −100 kV step by step, so that every strip sits on the ideal linear potential and the field stays uniform over the 2.5 m drift; skirt electrodes near the readout plane correct the end field. The gas system runs as a closed, continuously purified loop with oxygen and water held at ppm level, because electrons attach to electronegative molecules and vanish, and drift velocity shifts with E/N, temperature and pressure. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Field cage and resistor chain”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 165 條帶、15 mm 間距（教學值）估算：每級電壓 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V，正是 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm；若電阻鏈總阻值 4.1 GΩ，鏈電流 I ≈ 24 µA、功耗 2.4 W；單一電阻 1% 的誤差讓該級多出約 6 V，在一個間距內形成 1% 的局部場畸變。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Taking 165 strips at 15 mm pitch (teaching values): each step is 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V, exactly 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm; with a total chain resistance of 4.1 GΩ the chain current is I ≈ 24 µA and the dissipation 2.4 W; a 1% error in one resistor adds about 6 V to that step, a 1% local field distortion over one pitch.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「場籠與電阻鏈」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Field cage and resistor chain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-09-k1","title":"場籠、高壓與氣體純度","titleEn":"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity","text":"場籠用鍍鋁 Mylar 條帶環繞漂移體積，由電阻鏈把 −100 kV 逐級分壓，讓每一條帶的電位落在理想的線性分佈上，電場才能在 2.5 m 的全長保持均勻；靠近讀出面另有裙狀電極修正端部場。氣體系統以閉迴路循環並連續純化，氧與水必須壓在 ppm 等級，否則電子被電負性分子吸附而消失，而且漂移速度會隨 E/N、溫度與壓力改變。","textEn":"The field cage surrounds the drift volume with aluminised Mylar strips whose potentials are set by a resistor chain dividing the −100 kV step by step, so that every strip sits on the ideal linear potential and the field stays uniform over the 2.5 m drift; skirt electrodes near the readout plane correct the end field. The gas system runs as a closed, continuously purified loop with oxygen and water held at ppm level, because electrons attach to electronegative molecules and vanish, and drift velocity shifts with E/N, temperature and pressure.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「場籠、高壓與氣體純度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity\" is correct?","options":["場籠用鍍鋁 Mylar 條帶環繞漂移體積，由電阻鏈把 −100 kV 逐級分壓，讓每一條帶的電位落在理想的線性分佈上，電場才能在 2.5 m 的全長保持均勻。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。","氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["The field cage surrounds the drift volume with aluminised Mylar strips whose potentials are set by a resistor chain dividing the −100 kV step by step, so that every strip sits on the ideal linear potential and the field stays uniform over the 2.5 m drift.","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.","Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"場籠用鍍鋁 Mylar 條帶環繞漂移體積，由電阻鏈把 −100 kV 逐級分壓，讓每一條帶的電位落在理想的線性分佈上，電場才能在 2.5 m 的全長保持均勻；靠近讀出面另有裙狀電極修正端部場。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The field cage surrounds the drift volume with aluminised Mylar strips whose potentials are set by a resistor chain dividing the −100 kV step by step, so that every strip sits on the ideal linear potential and the field stays uniform over the 2.5 m drift; skirt electrodes near the readout plane correct the end field. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a466-v12-10","title":"場籠、高壓與氣體純度：定量估算","titleEn":"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「場籠與電阻鏈」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Field cage and resistor chain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 165 條帶、15 mm 間距（教學值）估算：每級電壓 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V，正是 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm；若電阻鏈總阻值 4.1 GΩ，鏈電流 I ≈ 24 µA、功耗 2.4 W；單一電阻 1% 的誤差讓該級多出約 6 V，在一個間距內形成 1% 的局部場畸變。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Taking 165 strips at 15 mm pitch (teaching values): each step is 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V, exactly 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm; with a total chain resistance of 4.1 GΩ the chain current is I ≈ 24 µA and the dissipation 2.4 W; a 1% error in one resistor adds about 6 V to that step, a 1% local field distortion over one pitch. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：量測各分壓節點電位（或電阻鏈各段阻值）並與線性目標比較；以氧分析儀與露點計監測 O₂ 與 H₂O，用 Goofie 型漂移速度監測器連續記錄 v_d；最後用雷射直線軌跡的殘差檢查場均勻性與 E×B 畸變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure every divider node (or each chain segment) against the linear target; monitor O₂ and H₂O with an oxygen analyser and a dew-point meter, record v_d continuously with a Goofie-type drift-velocity monitor, and finally check field uniformity and E×B distortion from residuals of straight laser tracks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 165 條帶、15 mm 間距（教學值）估算：每級電壓 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V，正是 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm；若電阻鏈總阻值 4.1 GΩ，鏈電流 I ≈ 24 µA、功耗 2.4 W；單一電阻 1% 的誤差讓該級多出約 6 V，在一個間距內形成 1% 的局部場畸變。","textEn":"Taking 165 strips at 15 mm pitch (teaching values): each step is 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V, exactly 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm; with a total chain resistance of 4.1 GΩ the chain current is I ≈ 24 µA and the dissipation 2.4 W; a 1% error in one resistor adds about 6 V to that step, a 1% local field distortion over one pitch.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「場籠、高壓與氣體純度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity\", which statement holds?","options":["對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。","以 165 條帶、15 mm 間距（教學值）估算：每級電壓 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V，正是 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm。","每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.","Taking 165 strips at 15 mm pitch (teaching values): each step is 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V, exactly 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm.","If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以 165 條帶、15 mm 間距（教學值）估算：每級電壓 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V，正是 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm；若電阻鏈總阻值 4.1 GΩ，鏈電流 I ≈ 24 µA、功耗 2.4 W；單一電阻 1% 的誤差讓該級多出約 6 V，在一個間距內形成 1% 的局部場畸變。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Taking 165 strips at 15 mm pitch (teaching values): each step is 100 kV/165 ≈ 606 V, exactly 400 V/cm × 1.5 cm; with a total chain resistance of 4.1 GΩ the chain current is I ≈ 24 µA and the dissipation 2.4 W; a 1% error in one resistor adds about 6 V to that step, a 1% local field distortion over one pitch. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a466-v12-11","title":"場籠、高壓與氣體純度：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「場籠與電阻鏈」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Field cage and resistor chain” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"量測各分壓節點電位（或電阻鏈各段阻值）並與線性目標比較；以氧分析儀與露點計監測 O₂ 與 H₂O，用 Goofie 型漂移速度監測器連續記錄 v_d；最後用雷射直線軌跡的殘差檢查場均勻性與 E×B 畸變。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure every divider node (or each chain segment) against the linear target; monitor O₂ and H₂O with an oxygen analyser and a dew-point meter, record v_d continuously with a Goofie-type drift-velocity monitor, and finally check field uniformity and E×B distortion from residuals of straight laser tracks. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：場籠內一次微放電或一顆漂移的電阻會使局部電位偏離，該區的電子被徑向推移，軌跡出現系統性的弓形殘差；若洩漏讓氧升到數十 ppm，遠端漂移的信號明顯衰減。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A micro-discharge or a drifting resistor shifts the local potential, electrons there are pushed radially and tracks show systematic bow-shaped residuals; a leak raising oxygen to tens of ppm visibly attenuates long-drift signals.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測各分壓節點電位（或電阻鏈各段阻值）並與線性目標比較；以氧分析儀與露點計監測 O₂ 與 H₂O，用 Goofie 型漂移速度監測器連續記錄 v_d；最後用雷射直線軌跡的殘差檢查場均勻性與 E×B 畸變。","textEn":"Measure every divider node (or each chain segment) against the linear target; monitor O₂ and H₂O with an oxygen analyser and a dew-point meter, record v_d continuously with a Goofie-type drift-velocity monitor, and finally check field uniformity and E×B distortion from residuals of straight laser tracks.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「場籠、高壓與氣體純度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","量測各分壓節點電位（或電阻鏈各段阻值）並與線性目標比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","Measure every divider node (or each chain segment) against the linear target."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測各分壓節點電位（或電阻鏈各段阻值）並與線性目標比較；以氧分析儀與露點計監測 O₂ 與 H₂O，用 Goofie 型漂移速度監測器連續記錄 v_d；最後用雷射直線軌跡的殘差檢查場均勻性與 E×B 畸變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure every divider node (or each chain segment) against the linear target; monitor O₂ and H₂O with an oxygen analyser and a dew-point meter, record v_d continuously with a Goofie-type drift-velocity monitor, and finally check field uniformity and E×B distortion from residuals of straight laser tracks. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a466-v12-12","title":"場籠、高壓與氣體純度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「場籠與電阻鏈」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Field cage and resistor chain” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"場籠內一次微放電或一顆漂移的電阻會使局部電位偏離，該區的電子被徑向推移，軌跡出現系統性的弓形殘差；若洩漏讓氧升到數十 ppm，遠端漂移的信號明顯衰減。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A micro-discharge or a drifting resistor shifts the local potential, electrons there are pushed radially and tracks show systematic bow-shaped residuals; a leak raising oxygen to tens of ppm visibly attenuates long-drift signals. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：氣體系統以閉迴路循環並連續純化，氧與水必須壓在 ppm 等級，否則電子被電負性分子吸附而消失，而且漂移速度會隨 E/N、溫度與壓力改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The gas system runs as a closed, continuously purified loop with oxygen and water held at ppm level, because electrons attach to electronegative molecules and vanish, and drift velocity shifts with E/N, temperature and pressure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"場籠內一次微放電或一顆漂移的電阻會使局部電位偏離，該區的電子被徑向推移，軌跡出現系統性的弓形殘差；若洩漏讓氧升到數十 ppm，遠端漂移的信號明顯衰減。","textEn":"A micro-discharge or a drifting resistor shifts the local potential, electrons there are pushed radially and tracks show systematic bow-shaped residuals; a leak raising oxygen to tens of ppm visibly attenuates long-drift signals.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「場籠、高壓與氣體純度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Field cage, high voltage and gas purity\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["場籠內一次微放電或一顆漂移的電阻會使局部電位偏離，該區的電子被徑向推移，軌跡出現系統性的弓形殘差；若洩漏讓氧升到數十 ppm，遠端漂移的信號明顯衰減。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["A micro-discharge or a drifting resistor shifts the local potential, electrons there are pushed radially and tracks show systematic bow-shaped residuals.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"場籠內一次微放電或一顆漂移的電阻會使局部電位偏離，該區的電子被徑向推移，軌跡出現系統性的弓形殘差；若洩漏讓氧升到數十 ppm，遠端漂移的信號明顯衰減。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A micro-discharge or a drifting resistor shifts the local potential, electrons there are pushed radially and tracks show systematic bow-shaped residuals; a leak raising oxygen to tens of ppm visibly attenuates long-drift signals. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a466-v12-13","title":"GEM 氣體增益與離子回流：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「四層 GEM 讀出室」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Four-GEM readout chambers” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"讀出室把漂移來的電子送進 50 µm 厚、佈滿 70 µm 微孔的 GEM 箔，孔內數十 kV/cm 的場讓電子雪崩倍增。ALICE 在 Run 3 把每個讀出室做成四層 GEM 疊（標準孔距與大孔距交替），總增益約 2000，同時把離子回流壓到 1% 以下，取代了需要閘極柵而產生死時間的多絲正比室，才能在 50 kHz 的鉛鉛碰撞率下連續讀出。雪崩的統計漲落與第一層 GEM 的電子收集效率共同決定能量解析度。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「四層 GEM 讀出室」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The readout chambers feed drifted electrons into 50 µm thick GEM foils pierced with 70 µm holes, where fields of tens of kV/cm drive avalanche multiplication. For Run 3 ALICE built each chamber as a four-GEM stack alternating standard and large-pitch foils, giving a total gain of about 2000 while holding ion back-flow below 1%; this replaced the multiwire chambers whose gating grid created dead time, and allows continuous readout at the 50 kHz Pb–Pb collision rate. Avalanche statistics together with electron collection efficiency in the first GEM set the energy resolution. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Four-GEM readout chambers”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：回流離子數 = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 個離子／初級電子；理想能量解析度 σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N)，取 F = 0.2、b = 0.6、N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155，得約 7%；實測約 12% 代表有效電子數只剩 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 個，即第一層 GEM 的有效透過率約 36%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Back-flowing ions = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 ions per primary electron; the ideal energy resolution σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N) with F = 0.2, b = 0.6 and N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155 is about 7%; a measured 12% implies only 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 effective electrons, i.e. an effective transparency of about 36% in the first GEM.","failure":"常見誤解：「氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「四層 GEM 讀出室」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Four-GEM readout chambers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-13-k1","title":"GEM 氣體增益與離子回流","titleEn":"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow","text":"讀出室把漂移來的電子送進 50 µm 厚、佈滿 70 µm 微孔的 GEM 箔，孔內數十 kV/cm 的場讓電子雪崩倍增。ALICE 在 Run 3 把每個讀出室做成四層 GEM 疊（標準孔距與大孔距交替），總增益約 2000，同時把離子回流壓到 1% 以下，取代了需要閘極柵而產生死時間的多絲正比室，才能在 50 kHz 的鉛鉛碰撞率下連續讀出。","textEn":"The readout chambers feed drifted electrons into 50 µm thick GEM foils pierced with 70 µm holes, where fields of tens of kV/cm drive avalanche multiplication. For Run 3 ALICE built each chamber as a four-GEM stack alternating standard and large-pitch foils, giving a total gain of about 2000 while holding ion back-flow below 1%; this replaced the multiwire chambers whose gating grid created dead time, and allows continuous readout at the 50 kHz Pb–Pb collision rate.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「GEM 氣體增益與離子回流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow\" is correct?","options":["氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。","讀出室把漂移來的電子送進 50 µm 厚、佈滿 70 µm 微孔的 GEM 箔，孔內數十 kV/cm 的場讓電子雪崩倍增。","漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。"],"optionsEn":["Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.","The readout chambers feed drifted electrons into 50 µm thick GEM foils pierced with 70 µm holes, where fields of tens of kV/cm drive avalanche multiplication.","Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"讀出室把漂移來的電子送進 50 µm 厚、佈滿 70 µm 微孔的 GEM 箔，孔內數十 kV/cm 的場讓電子雪崩倍增。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The readout chambers feed drifted electrons into 50 µm thick GEM foils pierced with 70 µm holes, where fields of tens of kV/cm drive avalanche multiplication. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a466-v12-14","title":"GEM 氣體增益與離子回流：定量估算","titleEn":"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「四層 GEM 讀出室」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Four-GEM readout chambers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：回流離子數 = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 個離子／初級電子；理想能量解析度 σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N)，取 F = 0.2、b = 0.6、N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155，得約 7%；實測約 12% 代表有效電子數只剩 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 個，即第一層 GEM 的有效透過率約 36%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Back-flowing ions = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 ions per primary electron; the ideal energy resolution σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N) with F = 0.2, b = 0.6 and N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155 is about 7%; a measured 12% implies only 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 effective electrons, i.e. an effective transparency of about 36% in the first GEM. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用 ⁵⁵Fe 的 5.9 keV X 光量每個讀出室的增益與能量解析度；以保護電極上陰極電流對陽極電流的比值量離子回流；掃描各層 GEM 電壓畫出增益對 IBF 的折衷曲線，並以長期測試確認工作點的放電率可接受。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure gain and energy resolution per chamber with 5.9 keV ⁵⁵Fe X-rays; measure ion back-flow as the ratio of cathode to anode current on the protection electrodes; scan the individual GEM voltages to map the gain-versus-IBF trade-off, and confirm in long-term tests that the discharge rate at the chosen working point is acceptable.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"回流離子數 = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 個離子／初級電子；理想能量解析度 σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N)，取 F = 0.2、b = 0.6、N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155，得約 7%；實測約 12% 代表有效電子數只剩 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 個，即第一層 GEM 的有效透過率約 36%。","textEn":"Back-flowing ions = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 ions per primary electron; the ideal energy resolution σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N) with F = 0.2, b = 0.6 and N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155 is about 7%; a measured 12% implies only 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 effective electrons, i.e. an effective transparency of about 36% in the first GEM.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「GEM 氣體增益與離子回流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow\", which statement holds?","options":["連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。","電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","回流離子數 = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 個離子／初級電子。"],"optionsEn":["Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed.","Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","Back-flowing ions = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 ions per primary electron."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回流離子數 = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 個離子／初級電子；理想能量解析度 σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N)，取 F = 0.2、b = 0.6、N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155，得約 7%；實測約 12% 代表有效電子數只剩 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 個，即第一層 GEM 的有效透過率約 36%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Back-flowing ions = G×IBF = 2000×0.007 = 14 ions per primary electron; the ideal energy resolution σ_E/E = √((F+b)/N) with F = 0.2, b = 0.6 and N = 5.9 keV/38 eV ≈ 155 is about 7%; a measured 12% implies only 0.8/0.12² ≈ 56 effective electrons, i.e. an effective transparency of about 36% in the first GEM. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a466-v12-15","title":"GEM 氣體增益與離子回流：量測與驗證","titleEn":"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「四層 GEM 讀出室」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Four-GEM readout chambers” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用 ⁵⁵Fe 的 5.9 keV X 光量每個讀出室的增益與能量解析度；以保護電極上陰極電流對陽極電流的比值量離子回流；掃描各層 GEM 電壓畫出增益對 IBF 的折衷曲線，並以長期測試確認工作點的放電率可接受。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure gain and energy resolution per chamber with 5.9 keV ⁵⁵Fe X-rays; measure ion back-flow as the ratio of cathode to anode current on the protection electrodes; scan the individual GEM voltages to map the gain-versus-IBF trade-off, and confirm in long-term tests that the discharge rate at the chosen working point is acceptable. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：為了改善能量解析度而調高第一層 GEM 電壓，離子回流隨之上升，高碰撞率下空間電荷畸變失控；反之壓得太低則透過率下降、dE/dx 解析度變差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Raising the first-GEM voltage to improve energy resolution raises ion back-flow and lets space-charge distortion run away at high rate; pushing it too low cuts transparency and worsens dE/dx resolution.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用 ⁵⁵Fe 的 5.9 keV X 光量每個讀出室的增益與能量解析度；以保護電極上陰極電流對陽極電流的比值量離子回流；掃描各層 GEM 電壓畫出增益對 IBF 的折衷曲線，並以長期測試確認工作點的放電率可接受。","textEn":"Measure gain and energy resolution per chamber with 5.9 keV ⁵⁵Fe X-rays; measure ion back-flow as the ratio of cathode to anode current on the protection electrodes; scan the individual GEM voltages to map the gain-versus-IBF trade-off, and confirm in long-term tests that the discharge rate at the chosen working point is acceptable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「GEM 氣體增益與離子回流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow\"?","options":["用 ⁵⁵Fe 的 5.9 keV X 光量每個讀出室的增益與能量解析度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Measure gain and energy resolution per chamber with 5.9 keV ⁵⁵Fe X-rays.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用 ⁵⁵Fe 的 5.9 keV X 光量每個讀出室的增益與能量解析度；以保護電極上陰極電流對陽極電流的比值量離子回流；掃描各層 GEM 電壓畫出增益對 IBF 的折衷曲線，並以長期測試確認工作點的放電率可接受。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure gain and energy resolution per chamber with 5.9 keV ⁵⁵Fe X-rays; measure ion back-flow as the ratio of cathode to anode current on the protection electrodes; scan the individual GEM voltages to map the gain-versus-IBF trade-off, and confirm in long-term tests that the discharge rate at the chosen working point is acceptable. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a466-v12-16","title":"GEM 氣體增益與離子回流：失效診斷","titleEn":"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「四層 GEM 讀出室」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Four-GEM readout chambers” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"為了改善能量解析度而調高第一層 GEM 電壓，離子回流隨之上升，高碰撞率下空間電荷畸變失控；反之壓得太低則透過率下降、dE/dx 解析度變差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Raising the first-GEM voltage to improve energy resolution raises ion back-flow and lets space-charge distortion run away at high rate; pushing it too low cuts transparency and worsens dE/dx resolution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：雪崩的統計漲落與第一層 GEM 的電子收集效率共同決定能量解析度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Avalanche statistics together with electron collection efficiency in the first GEM set the energy resolution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了改善能量解析度而調高第一層 GEM 電壓，離子回流隨之上升，高碰撞率下空間電荷畸變失控；反之壓得太低則透過率下降、dE/dx 解析度變差。","textEn":"Raising the first-GEM voltage to improve energy resolution raises ion back-flow and lets space-charge distortion run away at high rate; pushing it too low cuts transparency and worsens dE/dx resolution.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「GEM 氣體增益與離子回流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"GEM gas gain and ion back-flow\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","為了改善能量解析度而調高第一層 GEM 電壓，離子回流隨之上升，高碰撞率下空間電荷畸變失控；反之壓得太低則透過率下降、dE/dx 解析度變差。","漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Raising the first-GEM voltage to improve energy resolution raises ion back-flow and lets space-charge distortion run away at high rate.","Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為了改善能量解析度而調高第一層 GEM 電壓，離子回流隨之上升，高碰撞率下空間電荷畸變失控；反之壓得太低則透過率下降、dE/dx 解析度變差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Raising the first-GEM voltage to improve energy resolution raises ion back-flow and lets space-charge distortion run away at high rate; pushing it too low cuts transparency and worsens dE/dx resolution. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a466-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正」與「增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration\" and \"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a466-v12-17","title":"漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「雷射校正與畸變圖」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Laser calibration and distortion maps” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"要把到達時間換成 z，必須隨時掌握漂移速度；ALICE 用 266 nm 脈衝雷射經鏡組在腔內產生 336 條直線軌跡，並以獨立的漂移速度監測器追蹤氣體狀態。高碰撞率下回流的離子以約 1.6 cm/ms 緩慢漂移，在腔內累積成空間電荷，其徑向電場把漂移電子推離真實位置；畸變與離子密度成正比，必須用軌跡殘差或電流讀出建立隨時間更新的畸變圖加以修正。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「雷射校正與畸變圖」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Converting arrival time into z needs the drift velocity at all times; ALICE fires a pulsed 266 nm laser through mirror bundles to create 336 straight tracks inside the volume and follows gas condition with a separate drift-velocity monitor. At high rate the back-flowing ions drift slowly at about 1.6 cm/ms and accumulate as space charge whose radial field pushes drifting electrons off their true positions; the distortion scales with ion density and must be corrected with time-dependent maps built from track residuals or current readout. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Laser calibration and distortion maps”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：離子穿越時間 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms，50 kHz 鉛鉛碰撞下腔內同時存有約 8000 個事件的離子。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Ion transit time is 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms, so at 50 kHz Pb–Pb the ions of about 8000 events coexist in the volume.","failure":"常見誤解：「漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「雷射校正與畸變圖」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Laser calibration and distortion maps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-17-k1","title":"漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正","titleEn":"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration","text":"要把到達時間換成 z，必須隨時掌握漂移速度；ALICE 用 266 nm 脈衝雷射經鏡組在腔內產生 336 條直線軌跡，並以獨立的漂移速度監測器追蹤氣體狀態。高碰撞率下回流的離子以約 1.6 cm/ms 緩慢漂移，在腔內累積成空間電荷，其徑向電場把漂移電子推離真實位置；畸變與離子密度成正比，必須用軌跡殘差或電流讀出建立隨時間更新的畸變圖加以修正。","textEn":"Converting arrival time into z needs the drift velocity at all times; ALICE fires a pulsed 266 nm laser through mirror bundles to create 336 straight tracks inside the volume and follows gas condition with a separate drift-velocity monitor. At high rate the back-flowing ions drift slowly at about 1.6 cm/ms and accumulate as space charge whose radial field pushes drifting electrons off their true positions; the distortion scales with ion density and must be corrected with time-dependent maps built from track residuals or current readout.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration\" is correct?","options":["漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。","對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。","要把到達時間換成 z，必須隨時掌握漂移速度；ALICE 用 266 nm 脈衝雷射經鏡組在腔內產生 336 條直線軌跡，並以獨立的漂移速度監測器追蹤氣體狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough.","A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.","Converting arrival time into z needs the drift velocity at all times."],"answer":2,"explanation":"要把到達時間換成 z，必須隨時掌握漂移速度；ALICE 用 266 nm 脈衝雷射經鏡組在腔內產生 336 條直線軌跡，並以獨立的漂移速度監測器追蹤氣體狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Converting arrival time into z needs the drift velocity at all times; ALICE fires a pulsed 266 nm laser through mirror bundles to create 336 straight tracks inside the volume and follows gas condition with a separate drift-velocity monitor. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a466-v12-18","title":"漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正：定量估算","titleEn":"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雷射校正與畸變圖」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Laser calibration and distortion maps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：離子穿越時間 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms，50 kHz 鉛鉛碰撞下腔內同時存有約 8000 個事件的離子。取均勻離子密度 ρ = 2×10⁴ cm⁻³（教學假設）、半徑 1 m：E_r = ρe·r/(2ε₀) = 3.2×10⁻⁹ C/m³ × 1 m ÷ (2×8.85×10⁻¹² F/m) ≈ 180 V/m = 1.8 V/cm，E_r/E_z = 0.45%，全長漂移的徑向位移 ≈ 250 cm × 0.0045 ≈ 1.1 cm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Ion transit time is 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms, so at 50 kHz Pb–Pb the ions of about 8000 events coexist in the volume. For a uniform ion density ρ = 2×10⁴ cm⁻³ (teaching assumption) at radius 1 m, E_r = ρe·r/(2ε₀) = 3.2×10⁻⁹ C/m³ × 1 m ÷ (2×8.85×10⁻¹² F/m) ≈ 180 V/m = 1.8 V/cm, E_r/E_z = 0.45%, and a full-drift electron is displaced radially by ≈ 250 cm × 0.0045 ≈ 1.1 cm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：對幾何已知的雷射軌跡擬合直線並取殘差，分離漂移速度誤差（z 的線性縮放）與空間電荷畸變（隨 r、z 變化的徑向殘差）；把內層矽追蹤器外推的軌跡與 TPC 叢集比較，更新畸變圖，確認修正後殘差回到 1 mm 以下。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fit straight lines to laser tracks of known geometry and take residuals, separating drift-velocity error (a linear z scaling) from space-charge distortion (radial residuals varying with r and z); compare clusters with tracks extrapolated from the inner silicon tracker, update the distortion map and confirm that corrected residuals return below 1 mm.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"離子穿越時間 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms，50 kHz 鉛鉛碰撞下腔內同時存有約 8000 個事件的離子。取均勻離子密度 ρ = 2×10⁴ cm⁻³（教學假設）、半徑 1 m：E_r = ρe·r/(2ε₀) = 3.2×10⁻⁹ C/m³ × 1 m ÷ (2×8.85×10⁻¹² F/m) ≈ 180 V/m = 1.8 V/cm，E_r/E_z = 0.45%，全長漂移的徑向位移 ≈ 250 cm × 0.0045 ≈ 1.1 cm。","textEn":"Ion transit time is 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms, so at 50 kHz Pb–Pb the ions of about 8000 events coexist in the volume. For a uniform ion density ρ = 2×10⁴ cm⁻³ (teaching assumption) at radius 1 m, E_r = ρe·r/(2ε₀) = 3.2×10⁻⁹ C/m³ × 1 m ÷ (2×8.85×10⁻¹² F/m) ≈ 180 V/m = 1.8 V/cm, E_r/E_z = 0.45%, and a full-drift electron is displaced radially by ≈ 250 cm × 0.0045 ≈ 1.1 cm.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration\", which statement holds?","options":["離子穿越時間 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms，50 kHz 鉛鉛碰撞下腔內同時存有約 8000 個事件的離子。","每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。","磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Ion transit time is 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms, so at 50 kHz Pb–Pb the ions of about 8000 events coexist in the volume.","If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation.","The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"離子穿越時間 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms，50 kHz 鉛鉛碰撞下腔內同時存有約 8000 個事件的離子。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Ion transit time is 250 cm ÷ 1.6 cm/ms ≈ 160 ms, so at 50 kHz Pb–Pb the ions of about 8000 events coexist in the volume. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a466-v12-19","title":"漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「雷射校正與畸變圖」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Laser calibration and distortion maps” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"對幾何已知的雷射軌跡擬合直線並取殘差，分離漂移速度誤差（z 的線性縮放）與空間電荷畸變（隨 r、z 變化的徑向殘差）；把內層矽追蹤器外推的軌跡與 TPC 叢集比較，更新畸變圖，確認修正後殘差回到 1 mm 以下。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fit straight lines to laser tracks of known geometry and take residuals, separating drift-velocity error (a linear z scaling) from space-charge distortion (radial residuals varying with r and z); compare clusters with tracks extrapolated from the inner silicon tracker, update the distortion map and confirm that corrected residuals return below 1 mm. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若畸變圖更新慢於碰撞率的變化（例如束流強度在幾分鐘內下降），修正會過量或不足，表現為隨時間漂移的動量尺度與頂點偏移。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: If distortion maps update more slowly than the collision rate changes, for instance when beam intensity drops within minutes, the correction over- or under-shoots and appears as a time-dependent momentum scale and vertex offset.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對幾何已知的雷射軌跡擬合直線並取殘差，分離漂移速度誤差（z 的線性縮放）與空間電荷畸變（隨 r、z 變化的徑向殘差）；把內層矽追蹤器外推的軌跡與 TPC 叢集比較，更新畸變圖，確認修正後殘差回到 1 mm 以下。","textEn":"Fit straight lines to laser tracks of known geometry and take residuals, separating drift-velocity error (a linear z scaling) from space-charge distortion (radial residuals varying with r and z); compare clusters with tracks extrapolated from the inner silicon tracker, update the distortion map and confirm that corrected residuals return below 1 mm.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","對幾何已知的雷射軌跡擬合直線並取殘差，分離漂移速度誤差（z 的線性縮放）與空間電荷畸變（隨 r、z 變化的徑向殘差）。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Fit straight lines to laser tracks of known geometry and take residuals, separating drift-velocity error (a linear z scaling) from space-charge distortion (radial residuals varying with r and z).","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對幾何已知的雷射軌跡擬合直線並取殘差，分離漂移速度誤差（z 的線性縮放）與空間電荷畸變（隨 r、z 變化的徑向殘差）；把內層矽追蹤器外推的軌跡與 TPC 叢集比較，更新畸變圖，確認修正後殘差回到 1 mm 以下。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fit straight lines to laser tracks of known geometry and take residuals, separating drift-velocity error (a linear z scaling) from space-charge distortion (radial residuals varying with r and z); compare clusters with tracks extrapolated from the inner silicon tracker, update the distortion map and confirm that corrected residuals return below 1 mm. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a466-v12-20","title":"漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雷射校正與畸變圖」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Laser calibration and distortion maps” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若畸變圖更新慢於碰撞率的變化（例如束流強度在幾分鐘內下降），修正會過量或不足，表現為隨時間漂移的動量尺度與頂點偏移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"If distortion maps update more slowly than the collision rate changes, for instance when beam intensity drops within minutes, the correction over- or under-shoots and appears as a time-dependent momentum scale and vertex offset. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：高碰撞率下回流的離子以約 1.6 cm/ms 緩慢漂移，在腔內累積成空間電荷，其徑向電場把漂移電子推離真實位置；畸變與離子密度成正比，必須用軌跡殘差或電流讀出建立隨時間更新的畸變圖加以修正。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At high rate the back-flowing ions drift slowly at about 1.6 cm/ms and accumulate as space charge whose radial field pushes drifting electrons off their true positions; the distortion scales with ion density and must be corrected with time-dependent maps built from track residuals or current readout.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若畸變圖更新慢於碰撞率的變化（例如束流強度在幾分鐘內下降），修正會過量或不足，表現為隨時間漂移的動量尺度與頂點偏移。","textEn":"If distortion maps update more slowly than the collision rate changes, for instance when beam intensity drops within minutes, the correction over- or under-shoots and appears as a time-dependent momentum scale and vertex offset.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漂移速度、空間電荷與畸變校正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drift velocity, space charge and distortion calibration\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。","若畸變圖更新慢於碰撞率的變化（例如束流強度在幾分鐘內下降），修正會過量或不足，表現為隨時間漂移的動量尺度與頂點偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.","If distortion maps update more slowly than the collision rate changes, for instance when beam intensity drops within minutes, the correction over- or under-shoots and appears as a time-dependent momentum scale and vertex offset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若畸變圖更新慢於碰撞率的變化（例如束流強度在幾分鐘內下降），修正會過量或不足，表現為隨時間漂移的動量尺度與頂點偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If distortion maps update more slowly than the collision rate changes, for instance when beam intensity drops within minutes, the correction over- or under-shoots and appears as a time-dependent momentum scale and vertex offset. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a466-v12-21","title":"增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Krypton gain map and dE/dx” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"TPC 的第二項任務是用沿軌跡的能損 dE/dx 鑑別粒子：每一列墊片各量一次叢集電荷，152 列以截斷平均合併以壓制 Landau 分佈的長尾，再與 Bethe–Bloch 曲線比對。前提是每一塊墊片的增益都已知：ALICE 把放射性 ⁸³ᵐKr 注入氣體，其 41.6 keV 的衰變在整個腔內均勻發生，每塊墊片上的峰值位置就是該墊片的增益刻度。dE/dx 解析度由樣本數、樣本長度、增益校正品質與擴散共同決定。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The second job of a TPC is particle identification from energy loss along the track: each pad row measures one cluster charge, the 152 rows are combined as a truncated mean to suppress the Landau tail, and the result is compared with Bethe–Bloch curves. This requires the gain of every pad to be known: ALICE injects radioactive ⁸³ᵐKr into the gas, its 41.6 keV decays occur uniformly throughout the volume, and the peak position on each pad is that pad's gain scale. The dE/dx resolution then depends on sample count, sample length, gain-calibration quality and diffusion. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Krypton gain map and dE/dx”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：一次 ⁸³ᵐKr 衰變產生 N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 個初級電子，增益 2000 後約 2.2×10⁶ 個電子 ≈ 0.35 pC；若單一墊片的增益刻度不確定度為 2%，對 152 列截斷平均的貢獻只有 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16%，遠低於 5–6% 的總 dE/dx 解析度，但整列或整區的共同偏差不會被平均掉。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: One ⁸³ᵐKr decay yields N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 primary electrons, about 2.2×10⁶ electrons ≈ 0.35 pC after a gain of 2000; a 2% uncertainty in a single pad's gain contributes only 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16% to a 152-row truncated mean, far below the 5–6% total dE/dx resolution, whereas a common offset of a whole row or region is not averaged away.","failure":"常見誤解：「對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Krypton gain map and dE/dx”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-21-k1","title":"增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別","titleEn":"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification","text":"TPC 的第二項任務是用沿軌跡的能損 dE/dx 鑑別粒子：每一列墊片各量一次叢集電荷，152 列以截斷平均合併以壓制 Landau 分佈的長尾，再與 Bethe–Bloch 曲線比對。前提是每一塊墊片的增益都已知：ALICE 把放射性 ⁸³ᵐKr 注入氣體，其 41.6 keV 的衰變在整個腔內均勻發生，每塊墊片上的峰值位置就是該墊片的增益刻度。","textEn":"The second job of a TPC is particle identification from energy loss along the track: each pad row measures one cluster charge, the 152 rows are combined as a truncated mean to suppress the Landau tail, and the result is compared with Bethe–Bloch curves. This requires the gain of every pad to be known: ALICE injects radioactive ⁸³ᵐKr into the gas, its 41.6 keV decays occur uniformly throughout the volume, and the peak position on each pad is that pad's gain scale.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification\" is correct?","options":["TPC 的第二項任務是用沿軌跡的能損 dE/dx 鑑別粒子：每一列墊片各量一次叢集電荷，152 列以截斷平均合併以壓制 Landau 分佈的長尾，再與 Bethe–Bloch 曲線比對。","對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。","連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。"],"optionsEn":["The second job of a TPC is particle identification from energy loss along the track: each pad row measures one cluster charge, the 152 rows are combined as a truncated mean to suppress the Landau tail, and the result is compared with Bethe–Bloch curves.","A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.","Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"TPC 的第二項任務是用沿軌跡的能損 dE/dx 鑑別粒子：每一列墊片各量一次叢集電荷，152 列以截斷平均合併以壓制 Landau 分佈的長尾，再與 Bethe–Bloch 曲線比對。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The second job of a TPC is particle identification from energy loss along the track: each pad row measures one cluster charge, the 152 rows are combined as a truncated mean to suppress the Landau tail, and the result is compared with Bethe–Bloch curves. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a466-v12-22","title":"增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別：定量估算","titleEn":"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Krypton gain map and dE/dx” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：一次 ⁸³ᵐKr 衰變產生 N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 個初級電子，增益 2000 後約 2.2×10⁶ 個電子 ≈ 0.35 pC；若單一墊片的增益刻度不確定度為 2%，對 152 列截斷平均的貢獻只有 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16%，遠低於 5–6% 的總 dE/dx 解析度，但整列或整區的共同偏差不會被平均掉。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: One ⁸³ᵐKr decay yields N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 primary electrons, about 2.2×10⁶ electrons ≈ 0.35 pC after a gain of 2000; a 2% uncertainty in a single pad's gain contributes only 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16% to a 152-row truncated mean, far below the 5–6% total dE/dx resolution, whereas a common offset of a whole row or region is not averaged away. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：逐墊片擬合 Kr 峰建立增益圖，檢查其空間均勻性與隨時間的穩定度；用宇宙射線或低動量的質子、π、電子樣本擬合 Bethe–Bloch 參數，計算各動量區間的解析度與分離能力（以 σ 為單位的峰距）。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fit the Kr peak pad by pad to build the gain map and check its spatial uniformity and time stability; fit Bethe–Bloch parameters to dE/dx distributions of cosmic rays or low-momentum proton, pion and electron samples, and compute resolution and separation power (peak distance in units of σ) per momentum bin.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"一次 ⁸³ᵐKr 衰變產生 N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 個初級電子，增益 2000 後約 2.2×10⁶ 個電子 ≈ 0.35 pC；若單一墊片的增益刻度不確定度為 2%，對 152 列截斷平均的貢獻只有 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16%，遠低於 5–6% 的總 dE/dx 解析度，但整列或整區的共同偏差不會被平均掉。","textEn":"One ⁸³ᵐKr decay yields N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 primary electrons, about 2.2×10⁶ electrons ≈ 0.35 pC after a gain of 2000; a 2% uncertainty in a single pad's gain contributes only 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16% to a 152-row truncated mean, far below the 5–6% total dE/dx resolution, whereas a common offset of a whole row or region is not averaged away.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification\", which statement holds?","options":["電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","一次 ⁸³ᵐKr 衰變產生 N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 個初級電子，增益 2000 後約 2.2×10⁶ 個電子 ≈ 0.35 pC。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","One ⁸³ᵐKr decay yields N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 primary electrons, about 2.2×10⁶ electrons ≈ 0.35 pC after a gain of 2000.","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一次 ⁸³ᵐKr 衰變產生 N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 個初級電子，增益 2000 後約 2.2×10⁶ 個電子 ≈ 0.35 pC；若單一墊片的增益刻度不確定度為 2%，對 152 列截斷平均的貢獻只有 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16%，遠低於 5–6% 的總 dE/dx 解析度，但整列或整區的共同偏差不會被平均掉。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"One ⁸³ᵐKr decay yields N = 41,600 eV/38 eV ≈ 1095 primary electrons, about 2.2×10⁶ electrons ≈ 0.35 pC after a gain of 2000; a 2% uncertainty in a single pad's gain contributes only 2%/√152 ≈ 0.16% to a 152-row truncated mean, far below the 5–6% total dE/dx resolution, whereas a common offset of a whole row or region is not averaged away. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a466-v12-23","title":"增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Krypton gain map and dE/dx” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"逐墊片擬合 Kr 峰建立增益圖，檢查其空間均勻性與隨時間的穩定度；用宇宙射線或低動量的質子、π、電子樣本擬合 Bethe–Bloch 參數，計算各動量區間的解析度與分離能力（以 σ 為單位的峰距）。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fit the Kr peak pad by pad to build the gain map and check its spatial uniformity and time stability; fit Bethe–Bloch parameters to dE/dx distributions of cosmic rays or low-momentum proton, pion and electron samples, and compute resolution and separation power (peak distance in units of σ) per momentum bin. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：增益隨大氣壓每天漂移 1–2% 卻沒有參考信號追蹤時，整條 dE/dx 曲線上下移動，鑑別帶互相滲入，電子與 π 的誤判率上升。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: When gain drifts 1–2% per day with air pressure and no reference tracks it, the whole dE/dx curve shifts, identification bands leak into each other and electron–pion misidentification rises.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐墊片擬合 Kr 峰建立增益圖，檢查其空間均勻性與隨時間的穩定度；用宇宙射線或低動量的質子、π、電子樣本擬合 Bethe–Bloch 參數，計算各動量區間的解析度與分離能力（以 σ 為單位的峰距）。","textEn":"Fit the Kr peak pad by pad to build the gain map and check its spatial uniformity and time stability; fit Bethe–Bloch parameters to dE/dx distributions of cosmic rays or low-momentum proton, pion and electron samples, and compute resolution and separation power (peak distance in units of σ) per momentum bin.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。","逐墊片擬合 Kr 峰建立增益圖，檢查其空間均勻性與隨時間的穩定度。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.","Fit the Kr peak pad by pad to build the gain map and check its spatial uniformity and time stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐墊片擬合 Kr 峰建立增益圖，檢查其空間均勻性與隨時間的穩定度；用宇宙射線或低動量的質子、π、電子樣本擬合 Bethe–Bloch 參數，計算各動量區間的解析度與分離能力（以 σ 為單位的峰距）。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fit the Kr peak pad by pad to build the gain map and check its spatial uniformity and time stability; fit Bethe–Bloch parameters to dE/dx distributions of cosmic rays or low-momentum proton, pion and electron samples, and compute resolution and separation power (peak distance in units of σ) per momentum bin. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a466-v12-24","title":"增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「氪增益圖與 dE/dx」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Krypton gain map and dE/dx” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"增益隨大氣壓每天漂移 1–2% 卻沒有參考信號追蹤時，整條 dE/dx 曲線上下移動，鑑別帶互相滲入，電子與 π 的誤判率上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"When gain drifts 1–2% per day with air pressure and no reference tracks it, the whole dE/dx curve shifts, identification bands leak into each other and electron–pion misidentification rises. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：dE/dx 解析度由樣本數、樣本長度、增益校正品質與擴散共同決定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The dE/dx resolution then depends on sample count, sample length, gain-calibration quality and diffusion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"增益隨大氣壓每天漂移 1–2% 卻沒有參考信號追蹤時，整條 dE/dx 曲線上下移動，鑑別帶互相滲入，電子與 π 的誤判率上升。","textEn":"When gain drifts 1–2% per day with air pressure and no reference tracks it, the whole dE/dx curve shifts, identification bands leak into each other and electron–pion misidentification rises.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「增益均勻性、dE/dx 與粒子鑑別」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gain uniformity, dE/dx and particle identification\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["增益隨大氣壓每天漂移 1–2% 卻沒有參考信號追蹤時，整條 dE/dx 曲線上下移動，鑑別帶互相滲入，電子與 π 的誤判率上升。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。"],"optionsEn":["When gain drifts 1–2% per day with air pressure and no reference tracks it, the whole dE/dx curve shifts, identification bands leak into each other and electron–pion misidentification rises.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增益隨大氣壓每天漂移 1–2% 卻沒有參考信號追蹤時，整條 dE/dx 曲線上下移動，鑑別帶互相滲入，電子與 π 的誤判率上升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"When gain drifts 1–2% per day with air pressure and no reference tracks it, the whole dE/dx curve shifts, identification bands leak into each other and electron–pion misidentification rises. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a466-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「前端電子、連續讀出與資料流」與「試運轉、效能驗證與交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow\" and \"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a466-v12-25","title":"前端電子、連續讀出與資料流：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “SAMPA front end and readout chain” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"每塊墊片接到 SAMPA ASIC 的一個電荷靈敏前置放大與整形通道（每顆 32 通道、10 位元 ADC、5 MHz 取樣），約 160 ns 的整形時間與縱向擴散造成的 135 ns 時間展寬相稱。524,160 個通道把數位化波形經光纖連續送出，沒有觸發也沒有死時間，再由 FPGA 讀出卡扣除共模雜訊並做零抑制，才把資料率壓到可儲存的範圍。前端的雜訊、基線穩定度與通道間串音直接決定叢集電荷與位置的品質。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every pad feeds one charge-sensitive preamplifier–shaper channel of the SAMPA ASIC (32 channels per chip, 10-bit ADC, 5 MHz sampling), whose shaping time of about 160 ns matches the 135 ns time spread from longitudinal diffusion. The 524,160 channels stream digitised waveforms continuously over optical links, with no trigger and no dead time, and FPGA readout cards subtract common-mode noise and apply zero suppression to bring the data rate into a storable range. Front-end noise, baseline stability and channel-to-channel cross-talk directly set cluster-charge and position quality. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “SAMPA front end and readout chain”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原始資料率 = 524,160 通道 × 5×10⁶ 樣本/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s，與 ALICE 公布的數值一致；每列墊片約 30 個初級電子 × 增益 2000 = 6×10⁴ 個電子（9.6 fC），若前端等效雜訊電荷 ENC ≈ 670 個電子，單列訊噪比約 90。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Raw data rate = 524,160 channels × 5×10⁶ samples/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s, matching the figure ALICE publishes; a pad row with about 30 primary electrons × gain 2000 gives 6×10⁴ electrons (9.6 fC), and with a front-end equivalent noise charge ENC ≈ 670 electrons the per-row signal-to-noise ratio is about 90.","failure":"常見誤解：「連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “SAMPA front end and readout chain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-25-k1","title":"前端電子、連續讀出與資料流","titleEn":"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow","text":"每塊墊片接到 SAMPA ASIC 的一個電荷靈敏前置放大與整形通道（每顆 32 通道、10 位元 ADC、5 MHz 取樣），約 160 ns 的整形時間與縱向擴散造成的 135 ns 時間展寬相稱。524,160 個通道把數位化波形經光纖連續送出，沒有觸發也沒有死時間，再由 FPGA 讀出卡扣除共模雜訊並做零抑制，才把資料率壓到可儲存的範圍。","textEn":"Every pad feeds one charge-sensitive preamplifier–shaper channel of the SAMPA ASIC (32 channels per chip, 10-bit ADC, 5 MHz sampling), whose shaping time of about 160 ns matches the 135 ns time spread from longitudinal diffusion. The 524,160 channels stream digitised waveforms continuously over optical links, with no trigger and no dead time, and FPGA readout cards subtract common-mode noise and apply zero suppression to bring the data rate into a storable range.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「前端電子、連續讀出與資料流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow\" is correct?","options":["連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。","每塊墊片接到 SAMPA ASIC 的一個電荷靈敏前置放大與整形通道（每顆 32 通道、10 位元 ADC、5 MHz 取樣），約 160 ns 的整形時間與縱向擴散造成的 135 ns 時間展寬相稱。","每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed.","Every pad feeds one charge-sensitive preamplifier–shaper channel of the SAMPA ASIC (32 channels per chip, 10-bit ADC, 5 MHz sampling), whose shaping time of about 160 ns matches the 135 ns time spread from longitudinal diffusion.","If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每塊墊片接到 SAMPA ASIC 的一個電荷靈敏前置放大與整形通道（每顆 32 通道、10 位元 ADC、5 MHz 取樣），約 160 ns 的整形時間與縱向擴散造成的 135 ns 時間展寬相稱。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every pad feeds one charge-sensitive preamplifier–shaper channel of the SAMPA ASIC (32 channels per chip, 10-bit ADC, 5 MHz sampling), whose shaping time of about 160 ns matches the 135 ns time spread from longitudinal diffusion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a466-v12-26","title":"前端電子、連續讀出與資料流：定量估算","titleEn":"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “SAMPA front end and readout chain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原始資料率 = 524,160 通道 × 5×10⁶ 樣本/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s，與 ALICE 公布的數值一致；每列墊片約 30 個初級電子 × 增益 2000 = 6×10⁴ 個電子（9.6 fC），若前端等效雜訊電荷 ENC ≈ 670 個電子，單列訊噪比約 90。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Raw data rate = 524,160 channels × 5×10⁶ samples/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s, matching the figure ALICE publishes; a pad row with about 30 primary electrons × gain 2000 gives 6×10⁴ electrons (9.6 fC), and with a front-end equivalent noise charge ENC ≈ 670 electrons the per-row signal-to-noise ratio is about 90. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以內建的脈衝注入電容校正每通道的增益與基線，量 ENC（基線 RMS 換算成電子數）與通道間串音；無束流時記錄基線的共模成分並驗證扣除演算法；用光纖誤碼率與緩衝區佔用率確認讀出鏈在 50 kHz 碰撞率下不丟資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate gain and baseline per channel with the built-in pulse-injection capacitor, measure ENC (baseline RMS converted to electrons) and cross-talk; record common-mode baseline components without beam and validate the subtraction algorithm; confirm with link error rates and buffer occupancy that the readout chain drops no data at 50 kHz.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原始資料率 = 524,160 通道 × 5×10⁶ 樣本/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s，與 ALICE 公布的數值一致；每列墊片約 30 個初級電子 × 增益 2000 = 6×10⁴ 個電子（9.6 fC），若前端等效雜訊電荷 ENC ≈ 670 個電子，單列訊噪比約 90。","textEn":"Raw data rate = 524,160 channels × 5×10⁶ samples/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s, matching the figure ALICE publishes; a pad row with about 30 primary electrons × gain 2000 gives 6×10⁴ electrons (9.6 fC), and with a front-end equivalent noise charge ENC ≈ 670 electrons the per-row signal-to-noise ratio is about 90.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「前端電子、連續讀出與資料流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow\", which statement holds?","options":["磁場會同時壓低橫向與縱向擴散。","氣體增益越高，TPC 的軌跡與能損量測一定越好。","原始資料率 = 524,160 通道 × 5×10⁶ 樣本/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s，與 ALICE 公布的數值一致。"],"optionsEn":["The magnetic field suppresses both transverse and longitudinal diffusion.","Higher gas gain always gives better tracking and energy-loss measurement.","Raw data rate = 524,160 channels × 5×10⁶ samples/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s, matching the figure ALICE publishes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原始資料率 = 524,160 通道 × 5×10⁶ 樣本/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s，與 ALICE 公布的數值一致；每列墊片約 30 個初級電子 × 增益 2000 = 6×10⁴ 個電子（9.6 fC），若前端等效雜訊電荷 ENC ≈ 670 個電子，單列訊噪比約 90。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Raw data rate = 524,160 channels × 5×10⁶ samples/s × 10 bit ≈ 2.62×10¹³ bit/s ≈ 3.28 TB/s, matching the figure ALICE publishes; a pad row with about 30 primary electrons × gain 2000 gives 6×10⁴ electrons (9.6 fC), and with a front-end equivalent noise charge ENC ≈ 670 electrons the per-row signal-to-noise ratio is about 90. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a466-v12-27","title":"前端電子、連續讀出與資料流：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “SAMPA front end and readout chain” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以內建的脈衝注入電容校正每通道的增益與基線，量 ENC（基線 RMS 換算成電子數）與通道間串音；無束流時記錄基線的共模成分並驗證扣除演算法；用光纖誤碼率與緩衝區佔用率確認讀出鏈在 50 kHz 碰撞率下不丟資料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate gain and baseline per channel with the built-in pulse-injection capacitor, measure ENC (baseline RMS converted to electrons) and cross-talk; record common-mode baseline components without beam and validate the subtraction algorithm; confirm with link error rates and buffer occupancy that the readout chain drops no data at 50 kHz. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：共模雜訊未扣除時，低電荷叢集被零抑制門檻吃掉，軌跡在遠端漂移處出現斷點；整形時間過短則彈道虧損讓電荷被低估，dE/dx 系統性偏低。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Unsubtracted common-mode noise pushes low-charge clusters under the zero-suppression threshold so tracks break at long drift; too short a shaping time causes ballistic deficit, underestimating charge and biasing dE/dx low.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以內建的脈衝注入電容校正每通道的增益與基線，量 ENC（基線 RMS 換算成電子數）與通道間串音；無束流時記錄基線的共模成分並驗證扣除演算法；用光纖誤碼率與緩衝區佔用率確認讀出鏈在 50 kHz 碰撞率下不丟資料。","textEn":"Calibrate gain and baseline per channel with the built-in pulse-injection capacitor, measure ENC (baseline RMS converted to electrons) and cross-talk; record common-mode baseline components without beam and validate the subtraction algorithm; confirm with link error rates and buffer occupancy that the readout chain drops no data at 50 kHz.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「前端電子、連續讀出與資料流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow\"?","options":["以內建的脈衝注入電容校正每通道的增益與基線，量 ENC（基線 RMS 換算成電子數）與通道間串音。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。"],"optionsEn":["Calibrate gain and baseline per channel with the built-in pulse-injection capacitor, measure ENC (baseline RMS converted to electrons) and cross-talk.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以內建的脈衝注入電容校正每通道的增益與基線，量 ENC（基線 RMS 換算成電子數）與通道間串音；無束流時記錄基線的共模成分並驗證扣除演算法；用光纖誤碼率與緩衝區佔用率確認讀出鏈在 50 kHz 碰撞率下不丟資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate gain and baseline per channel with the built-in pulse-injection capacitor, measure ENC (baseline RMS converted to electrons) and cross-talk; record common-mode baseline components without beam and validate the subtraction algorithm; confirm with link error rates and buffer occupancy that the readout chain drops no data at 50 kHz. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a466-v12-28","title":"前端電子、連續讀出與資料流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「SAMPA 前端與讀出鏈」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “SAMPA front end and readout chain” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"共模雜訊未扣除時，低電荷叢集被零抑制門檻吃掉，軌跡在遠端漂移處出現斷點；整形時間過短則彈道虧損讓電荷被低估，dE/dx 系統性偏低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Unsubtracted common-mode noise pushes low-charge clusters under the zero-suppression threshold so tracks break at long drift; too short a shaping time causes ballistic deficit, underestimating charge and biasing dE/dx low. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：前端的雜訊、基線穩定度與通道間串音直接決定叢集電荷與位置的品質。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Front-end noise, baseline stability and channel-to-channel cross-talk directly set cluster-charge and position quality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「連續讀出沒有觸發，所以不需要時間校正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Continuous readout has no trigger, so no timing calibration is needed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共模雜訊未扣除時，低電荷叢集被零抑制門檻吃掉，軌跡在遠端漂移處出現斷點；整形時間過短則彈道虧損讓電荷被低估，dE/dx 系統性偏低。","textEn":"Unsubtracted common-mode noise pushes low-charge clusters under the zero-suppression threshold so tracks break at long drift; too short a shaping time causes ballistic deficit, underestimating charge and biasing dE/dx low.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「前端電子、連續讀出與資料流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Front-end electronics, continuous readout and data flow\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","共模雜訊未扣除時，低電荷叢集被零抑制門檻吃掉，軌跡在遠端漂移處出現斷點；整形時間過短則彈道虧損讓電荷被低估，dE/dx 系統性偏低。","每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Unsubtracted common-mode noise pushes low-charge clusters under the zero-suppression threshold so tracks break at long drift.","If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共模雜訊未扣除時，低電荷叢集被零抑制門檻吃掉，軌跡在遠端漂移處出現斷點；整形時間過短則彈道虧損讓電荷被低估，dE/dx 系統性偏低。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsubtracted common-mode noise pushes low-charge clusters under the zero-suppression threshold so tracks break at long drift; too short a shaping time causes ballistic deficit, underestimating charge and biasing dE/dx low. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a466-v12-29","title":"試運轉、效能驗證與交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「試運轉與校正資料庫」如何決定時間投影室偵測器的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Commissioning and calibration database” determines the key performance of “Time-projection-chamber detectors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"整機驗證從高壓訓練與氣密測試開始，接著用宇宙射線與雷射確認每個讀出室的效率與對準，再以 Kr 校正建立增益圖，最後在束流下量位置解析度、dE/dx 解析度與動量解析度，並把漂移速度、增益、畸變圖與對準參數連同版本號寫入校正資料庫。交接文件必須記錄工作點（各層 GEM 電壓、增益、IBF）、放電與高壓跳脫的統計，以及每一項效能指標的量測條件。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「試運轉與校正資料庫」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"System validation starts with high-voltage training and gas-tightness tests, continues with cosmic rays and lasers to confirm efficiency and alignment of every readout chamber, then builds the gain map with Kr calibration, and finally measures position, dE/dx and momentum resolution with beam, writing drift velocity, gain, distortion maps and alignment constants with version numbers into the calibration database. The handoff record must document the working point (GEM voltages, gain, IBF), discharge and HV-trip statistics, and the measurement conditions of every performance figure. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Commissioning and calibration database”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Gluckstern 估計 σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4))：取 σ_rφ = 0.8 mm、B = 0.5 T、L = 1.6 m、N = 152、pT = 10 GeV/c，得 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%，這就是單獨 TPC 在高動量區的解析度量級。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Gluckstern estimate σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4)): with σ_rφ = 0.8 mm, B = 0.5 T, L = 1.6 m, N = 152 and pT = 10 GeV/c this is 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%, the order of the stand-alone TPC resolution at high momentum.","failure":"常見誤解：「每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「試運轉與校正資料庫」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Commissioning and calibration database”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-29-k1","title":"試運轉、效能驗證與交接","titleEn":"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff","text":"整機驗證從高壓訓練與氣密測試開始，接著用宇宙射線與雷射確認每個讀出室的效率與對準，再以 Kr 校正建立增益圖，最後在束流下量位置解析度、dE/dx 解析度與動量解析度，並把漂移速度、增益、畸變圖與對準參數連同版本號寫入校正資料庫。交接文件必須記錄工作點（各層 GEM 電壓、增益、IBF）、放電與高壓跳脫的統計，以及每一項效能指標的量測條件。","textEn":"System validation starts with high-voltage training and gas-tightness tests, continues with cosmic rays and lasers to confirm efficiency and alignment of every readout chamber, then builds the gain map with Kr calibration, and finally measures position, dE/dx and momentum resolution with beam, writing drift velocity, gain, distortion maps and alignment constants with version numbers into the calibration database. The handoff record must document the working point (GEM voltages, gain, IBF), discharge and HV-trip statistics, and the measurement conditions of every performance figure.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試運轉、效能驗證與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff\" is correct?","options":["每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。","電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","整機驗證從高壓訓練與氣密測試開始，接著用宇宙射線與雷射確認每個讀出室的效率與對準，再以 Kr 校正建立增益圖，最後在束流下量位置解析度、dE/dx 解析度與動量解析度，並把漂移速度、增益、畸變圖與對準參數連同版本號寫入校正資料庫。"],"optionsEn":["If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation.","Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","System validation starts with high-voltage training and gas-tightness tests, continues with cosmic rays and lasers to confirm efficiency and alignment of every readout chamber, then builds the gain map with Kr calibration, and finally measures position, dE/dx and momentum resolution with beam, writing drift velocity, gain, distortion maps and alignment constants with version numbers into the calibration database."],"answer":2,"explanation":"整機驗證從高壓訓練與氣密測試開始，接著用宇宙射線與雷射確認每個讀出室的效率與對準，再以 Kr 校正建立增益圖，最後在束流下量位置解析度、dE/dx 解析度與動量解析度，並把漂移速度、增益、畸變圖與對準參數連同版本號寫入校正資料庫。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"System validation starts with high-voltage training and gas-tightness tests, continues with cosmic rays and lasers to confirm efficiency and alignment of every readout chamber, then builds the gain map with Kr calibration, and finally measures position, dE/dx and momentum resolution with beam, writing drift velocity, gain, distortion maps and alignment constants with version numbers into the calibration database. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a466-v12-30","title":"試運轉、效能驗證與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「試運轉與校正資料庫」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Commissioning and calibration database” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Gluckstern 估計 σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4))：取 σ_rφ = 0.8 mm、B = 0.5 T、L = 1.6 m、N = 152、pT = 10 GeV/c，得 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%，這就是單獨 TPC 在高動量區的解析度量級。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Gluckstern estimate σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4)): with σ_rφ = 0.8 mm, B = 0.5 T, L = 1.6 m, N = 152 and pT = 10 GeV/c this is 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%, the order of the stand-alone TPC resolution at high momentum. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：把宇宙射線軌跡切成上下兩半分別擬合，在交會處比較動量與位置差異以直接量解析度；用 K⁰ₛ 與 Λ 的不變質量寬度驗證動量尺度與解析度；核對校正資料庫中每個參數的生效區間與來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, fit each separately and compare momentum and position at the crossing point to measure resolution directly; verify momentum scale and resolution from the invariant-mass widths of K⁰ₛ and Λ; check validity intervals and provenance of every parameter in the calibration database.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Gluckstern 估計 σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4))：取 σ_rφ = 0.8 mm、B = 0.5 T、L = 1.6 m、N = 152、pT = 10 GeV/c，得 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%，這就是單獨 TPC 在高動量區的解析度量級。","textEn":"Gluckstern estimate σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4)): with σ_rφ = 0.8 mm, B = 0.5 T, L = 1.6 m, N = 152 and pT = 10 GeV/c this is 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%, the order of the stand-alone TPC resolution at high momentum.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「試運轉、效能驗證與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["Gluckstern 估計 σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4))：取 σ_rφ = 0.8 mm、B = 0.5 T、L = 1.6 m、N = 152、pT = 10 GeV/c，得 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%，這就是單獨 TPC 在高動量區的解析度量級。","只要中央電極電壓正確，漂移電場就自動均勻。","漂移速度在試運轉時量一次就夠用了。"],"optionsEn":["Gluckstern estimate σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4)): with σ_rφ = 0.8 mm, B = 0.5 T, L = 1.6 m, N = 152 and pT = 10 GeV/c this is 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%, the order of the stand-alone TPC resolution at high momentum.","If the central-electrode voltage is right, the drift field is automatically uniform.","Measuring the drift velocity once at commissioning is enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Gluckstern 估計 σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4))：取 σ_rφ = 0.8 mm、B = 0.5 T、L = 1.6 m、N = 152、pT = 10 GeV/c，得 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%，這就是單獨 TPC 在高動量區的解析度量級。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Gluckstern estimate σ_pT/pT ≈ σ_rφ·pT/(0.3·B·L²)·√(720/(N+4)): with σ_rφ = 0.8 mm, B = 0.5 T, L = 1.6 m, N = 152 and pT = 10 GeV/c this is 0.0008×10/(0.3×0.5×2.56) × √(720/156) ≈ 0.0208×2.15 ≈ 4.5%, the order of the stand-alone TPC resolution at high momentum. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a466-v12-31","title":"試運轉、效能驗證與交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「試運轉與校正資料庫」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Commissioning and calibration database” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"把宇宙射線軌跡切成上下兩半分別擬合，在交會處比較動量與位置差異以直接量解析度；用 K⁰ₛ 與 Λ 的不變質量寬度驗證動量尺度與解析度；核對校正資料庫中每個參數的生效區間與來源。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, fit each separately and compare momentum and position at the crossing point to measure resolution directly; verify momentum scale and resolution from the invariant-mass widths of K⁰ₛ and Λ; check validity intervals and provenance of every parameter in the calibration database. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：交接時沒有記錄校正常數的版本，之後的重建會混用不同時期的增益或畸變圖，重新處理的資料出現無法解釋的效能跳變。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: If calibration-constant versions are not recorded at handoff, later reconstruction mixes gain or distortion maps from different periods and reprocessed data show unexplained performance jumps.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把宇宙射線軌跡切成上下兩半分別擬合，在交會處比較動量與位置差異以直接量解析度；用 K⁰ₛ 與 Λ 的不變質量寬度驗證動量尺度與解析度；核對校正資料庫中每個參數的生效區間與來源。","textEn":"Split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, fit each separately and compare momentum and position at the crossing point to measure resolution directly; verify momentum scale and resolution from the invariant-mass widths of K⁰ₛ and Λ; check validity intervals and provenance of every parameter in the calibration database.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「試運轉、效能驗證與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","把宇宙射線軌跡切成上下兩半分別擬合，在交會處比較動量與位置差異以直接量解析度。","對所有列直接取平均就能得到最好的 dE/dx 解析度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, fit each separately and compare momentum and position at the crossing point to measure resolution directly.","A plain average over all rows gives the best dE/dx resolution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把宇宙射線軌跡切成上下兩半分別擬合，在交會處比較動量與位置差異以直接量解析度；用 K⁰ₛ 與 Λ 的不變質量寬度驗證動量尺度與解析度；核對校正資料庫中每個參數的生效區間與來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Split cosmic-ray tracks into upper and lower halves, fit each separately and compare momentum and position at the crossing point to measure resolution directly; verify momentum scale and resolution from the invariant-mass widths of K⁰ₛ and Λ; check validity intervals and provenance of every parameter in the calibration database. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a466-v12-32","title":"試運轉、效能驗證與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"prerequisiteIds":["a466-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「試運轉與校正資料庫」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Commissioning and calibration database” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"交接時沒有記錄校正常數的版本，之後的重建會混用不同時期的增益或畸變圖，重新處理的資料出現無法解釋的效能跳變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"If calibration-constant versions are not recorded at handoff, later reconstruction mixes gain or distortion maps from different periods and reprocessed data show unexplained performance jumps. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：交接文件必須記錄工作點（各層 GEM 電壓、增益、IBF）、放電與高壓跳脫的統計，以及每一項效能指標的量測條件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The handoff record must document the working point (GEM voltages, gain, IBF), discharge and HV-trip statistics, and the measurement conditions of every performance figure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每個讀出室在實驗室各自測試合格，整個 TPC 就不需要整機驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If each readout chamber passes lab tests, the whole TPC needs no system validation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a466-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"交接時沒有記錄校正常數的版本，之後的重建會混用不同時期的增益或畸變圖，重新處理的資料出現無法解釋的效能跳變。","textEn":"If calibration-constant versions are not recorded at handoff, later reconstruction mixes gain or distortion maps from different periods and reprocessed data show unexplained performance jumps.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]},{"id":"a466-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「試運轉、效能驗證與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Commissioning, performance validation and handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","電子沿電場一路加速到很高速度，所以漂移時間可以忽略。","交接時沒有記錄校正常數的版本，之後的重建會混用不同時期的增益或畸變圖，重新處理的資料出現無法解釋的效能跳變。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Electrons accelerate along the field to very high speed, so drift time can be ignored.","If calibration-constant versions are not recorded at handoff, later reconstruction mixes gain or distortion maps from different periods and reprocessed data show unexplained performance jumps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交接時沒有記錄校正常數的版本，之後的重建會混用不同時期的增益或畸變圖，重新處理的資料出現無法解釋的效能跳變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If calibration-constant versions are not recorded at handoff, later reconstruction mixes gain or distortion maps from different periods and reprocessed data show unexplained performance jumps. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v12o-alice-tpc","v12o-cern-gdd-gem","v12o-cern-alice"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
